# Differences from the two sides running different DWriteCore builds, not from
# anything the shim decides. Linux forwards to the Office drop in
# third_party/office-android; Windows loads the app-dir DWriteCore.dll from
# Windows App SDK 2.1.1.2605.
#
# avar2 design-space warping: the Office drop applies it, App SDK does not.
#
# Delete an entry once both sides run the same drop. A cell going quiet is not
# that condition: from milestone 148 Blink routes avar2 fonts to Fontations, so
# these match on Chromium 148 and up while still differing on CEF 144.
wt/external/wpt/css/css-fonts/variations/variable-avar2-warp.html
wt/external/wpt/css/css-fonts/variations/variable-avar2-rvrn.html
